<ContentControl x:Class="KomorebiDashboard.Views.TabLayout"
                xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                xmlns:views="clr-namespace:KomorebiDashboard.Views">
  <!--
    The standard tab body, as a ContentControl with a template rather than a
    UserControl. That is deliberate: a UserControl's content is already its own
    Grid, so a consumer setting child content would REPLACE that Grid and the
    console pane would vanish. With a ContentControl the consumer's content lands
    in the template's ContentPresenter, which is exactly the "layout with a slot"
    this is.

    A tab therefore reads as:

        <views:TabLayout PageTitle="Kill and Start" PageSubtitle="...">
          <StackPanel>
            <Border Style="{DynamicResource K1cRow}"> ... </Border>
          </StackPanel>
        </views:TabLayout>

    The console pane and the status line come from here, so no tab can render them
    differently — and the two star row heights come from the tab's ViewModel,
    which is where the persisted console percentage is applied.

    Row 0 Auto    heading + subtitle (never scrolls away)
    Row 1 *       the tab's rows (scrolls)
    Row 2 *       the shared console pane

    ShowConsole="False" removes the console pane and gives its share of the tab
    to the content row. It is a property of THIS control rather than something
    the tab's ViewModel must know about, because the tabs that have no console
    (Customization, About) are not TabViewModelBase and so have no ConsoleRowHeight
    to bind: the binding would fail silently and the rows would fall back to the
    default 1*, which is how an empty console used to appear on a tab that runs
    nothing. See ApplyConsoleVisibility in the code-behind.
  -->
  <ContentControl.Template>
    <ControlTemplate TargetType="ContentControl">
      <Grid x:Name="PART_Grid" Margin="16,14,16,12">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
          <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
          <RowDefinition x:Name="PART_ContentRow" Height="{Binding ContentRowHeight}" />
          <RowDefinition x:Name="PART_ConsoleRow" Height="{Binding ConsoleRowHeight}" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,0,0,12">
          <TextBlock Text="{Binding PageTitle, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                     Style="{DynamicResource K1cPageTitle}" />
          <TextBlock Text="{Binding PageSubtitle, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                     Style="{DynamicResource K1cPageSubtitle}" Margin="0,3,0,0" />
        </StackPanel>

        <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                      HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                      Padding="0,0,6,0">
          <ContentPresenter />
        </ScrollViewer>

        <views:ConsolePane x:Name="PART_Console" Grid.Row="2" />
      </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>
  </ContentControl.Template>
</ContentControl>